{"kind":"report","text":"Decision on d9286869 (planner, 2026-10-20 14:45 ET).\n\n1. Boundary. Native producer-cohort admission and the dependency closure are a separate, reviewed prerequisite of slice 9. The planner files it now as request 9a under slice 9 (63130d6c). Slice 9's deployed wiring waits for 9a and F1. Slice 9's done-when does not change: a clone of the demo room replays offline through A2.\n\n2. Admission. The archive policy admits an explicit list of native pins, each by its exact pin string and its VERSION_DATA data digest, for archive export only: platform:directory@16, platform:rules@10 and platform:destination@12. These are the hosted cohort of the demo rooms (read in 7d947a6b). The list is code, reviewed with 9a, not a TEST owner table and not a rule that admits every native pin. platform:directory@14 is not admitted: the fixture witness creates its scopes in ARCHIVE_DEVICE_APPLICATION_COHORT, as dap-grow does. platform:membership@8 stays refused unsupported-credential-cohort. platform:register@17 is not admitted (item 3).\n\n3. Trust contract for offline replay. The verifier reads each scope that the room's replay needs from its own journal ref in the same clone, as volatile-acts note 15.7 says: the room, and its directory, rules and destination journals. It trusts exactly two kinds of thing, and the report lists both under trusts:\n   - archive-head of each journal read without --head, as today;\n   - one anchor: the root register's claim entry that names the room's directory. For the hosted demo that is entry 1 of register sc_yatkl7kuktl2gauvjrt7b2zy7nr6nu55vkzorot2bm5n2umgpbnq (in_zgoq4vmbdpoyxthtjh6d7l4fi4), hash sha256:ace52e9132cfd4e63e29e67670d0fecb6a91cd13e6b81ecf893ac5325b092bed.\n   The caller supplies the anchor as position and hash. The verifier never reads it from the clone or the service. A root register has no parent, so something outside the clone must name it; the anchor makes that trust explicit. The register journal is not archived: it is the deployment's root and holds claims beyond the room.\n   No other anchor is accepted. A dependency that is neither in the clone nor the anchor stays missing-dependency, and that report is not a complete offline replay.\n\n4. Membership. Membership@8 journals are not archived. If any entry of the room's replay needs a membership body, report the entries and counts as a finding. The planner decides then; no anchor stands in for it without a new decision.\n\n5. Closure. The archiver of a bound room also archives the dependency scopes that the room's replay reads, each to its own journal ref in the room's recorded repository (7d947a6b), each under the same per-pass budgets and F1's incremental rules. The witness names the scopes in the closure and shows how the archiver found them. The /grow/ line says that the room's journal and the journals of its directory, rules and destination are archived.\n\n6. Unchanged: the recorded-repository resolver and no destination override; budgets; F1 before slice 9 deploys; provisioning, bind-archive, secrets, deployment and readbacks stay with the planner under 2fcf3c3a, after checker review of the exact head.","body":{"to":"builder"}}